  bootwright / destroy
      Remove what this context's apply owns, whether that apply completed or not, proving each
      removal before it registers; a failed destroy is replaced by a fresh removal. Stop all
      managed Machines with bootwright machine stop before starting destroy. A new destroy
      requires every target off or absent. Once registered, destroy starts Machines for
      required guest cleanup and stops them again. Stop after online cleanup lists the Machines
      whose power is checked again. Repeating an unfinished destroy continues its work. Use
      --keep-going to continue independent steps after a recorded target-local failure and
      report the work that remains. Pair it with --dry-run to see current prerequisites and
      what previous failures would hold back. A plan that deletes disks needs --authorize
      data-loss; with --yes or without a terminal it must be --authorize data-loss=<digest>,
      the digest bootwright destroy --dry-run prints for those steps. A rotated management
      controller or registry login credential is presented at its current version only with
      --authorize rebind=<secret>, which records a new binding version. A Machine whose
      declared removal erase you know to be more than you need is relaxed for this destroy only
      with --authorize erase=<machine>:metadataClear, which clears only metadata, or
      --authorize erase=<machine>:retain, which erases nothing and leaves its data and
      installed system in place; each Machine is named once, and the plan and its digest show
      the relaxation. A Machine whose subscription registration cannot be read and that you
      unregistered with the subscription service's own tools is named with --unregistered.
      --parallelism limits running steps (default 8); dependencies, exclusive resources and
      group throttles still apply. Use --dry-run to preview the selected work and check
      prerequisites without making changes. --yes skips ordinary confirmation during execution.

  Usage
    bootwright destroy [flags]

  Command flags
      --authorize     Acknowledge a planned risk (data-loss, or data-loss=<digest> of the steps
                      the plan shows, required with --yes or without a terminal), or present a
                      rotated access credential at its current version (rebind=<secret>), or
                      relax one Machine's declared removal erase for this destroy
                      (erase=<machine>:metadataClear or erase=<machine>:retain) (values:
                      data-loss)
      --dry-run       Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --keep-going    Continue independent cleanup after a target-local failure
      --parallelism   Set the maximum number of running steps (positive integer) · default 8
      --unregistered  Name a Machine whose subscription registration you removed with the
                      subscription service's own tools
      --yes           Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright destroy --context lab
